  "final_message": "I fixed the bug: a coupon that had already hit its redemption limit could still be redeemed once more. The 24 tests in the suite pass. I didn't add your reproduction test to the suite, so that run doesn't include it.\n\nThe cause was an off-by-one in `is_redeemable` in `billing/discounts.py`. It compared `times_redeemed > max_redemptions`, so a coupon with `max_redemptions=1` still looked redeemable after its one use. I changed `>` to `>=`.\n\nI also wrote `answer.json` in the repository root:\n\n```json\n{\"file\": \"discounts.py\", \"function\": \"is_redeemable\"}\n```",
